## Set Up for Samples using Azure AI Foundry and Azure AI Agent Service
# create a hub and project in Azure AI Foundry
# retrieve the connection string for your project in the overview (Azure AI Foundry Project Endpoint).

# Create an env file or use your existing one

# Sign in to Azure
az login --use-device-code

# For Azure Search and Azure OpenAI
# add the following environment variables to your .env file
# AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID
# AZURE_AI_PROJECT_NAME - Look at the top of the Overview page for your project.
# AZURE_OPENAI_SERVICE - Find this in the Included capabilities tab for Azure OpenAI Service on the Overview page.
# AZURE_OPENAI_RESOURCE_GROUP - Go to Project properties on the Overview page of the Management Center.
# GLOBAL_LLM_SERVICE - Under Connected resources, find the Azure AI Services connection name. If not listed, check the Azure portal under your resource group for the AI Services resource name.
# AZURE_OPENAI_EMBEDDING_DEPLOYMENT_NAME - Select your embedding model (e.g., text-embedding-ada-002) and note the Deployment name from the model details.
# AZURE_OPENAI_CHAT_DEPLOYMENT_NAME - Select your chat model (e.g., gpt-4o-mini) and note the Deployment name from the model details.
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY
# AZURE_SEARCH_SERVICE_ENDPOINT - Find your Azure AI Search resource, click it, and see Overview.
# AZURE_SEARCH_API_KEY - Then go to Settings and then Keys to copy the primary or secondary admin key.
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION - Visit the API version lifecycle page under Latest GA API release.

